From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: mzak <mzak.amin@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 10 Oct 2026 18:23:42 +0300
Subject: [PATCH] firmware: arm_scmi: put the P2A CHANNEL_FREE quirk code in a
 QUIRK_ macro

The quirk of the previous commit passed its code block straight to
SCMI_QUIRK(), so the statement expression's '({' and '})' came from
different macro expansions and clang warned twice
(-Wcompound-token-split-by-macro, also without W=1). Define the block as
QUIRK_P2A_NO_CHANNEL_FREE_ACK, the way the existing quirks do
(QUIRK_PERF_FC_FORCE, QUIRK_OUT_OF_SPEC_TRIPLET). No functional change.

Signed-off-by: mzak <mzak.amin@gmail.com>
---
 drivers/firmware/arm_scmi/driver.c | 6 ++++--
 1 file changed, 4 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/firmware/arm_scmi/driver.c b/drivers/firmware/arm_scmi/driver.c
index b155571edc9d..434a997c8c67 100644
--- a/drivers/firmware/arm_scmi/driver.c
+++ b/drivers/firmware/arm_scmi/driver.c
@@ -1064,6 +1064,9 @@ static inline void scmi_xfer_command_release(struct scmi_info *info,
 	__scmi_xfer_put(&info->tx_minfo, xfer);
 }
 
+/* Platform does not consume the P2A CHANNEL_FREE ack: skip the write */
+#define QUIRK_P2A_NO_CHANNEL_FREE_ACK						({										return;								})
+
 static inline void scmi_clear_channel(struct scmi_info *info,
 				      struct scmi_chan_info *cinfo)
 {
@@ -1072,8 +1075,7 @@ static inline void scmi_clear_channel(struct scmi_info *info,
 		return;
 	}
 
-	/* Platform does not consume the P2A CHANNEL_FREE ack; skip the write */
-	SCMI_QUIRK(p2a_no_channel_free_ack, { return; });
+	SCMI_QUIRK(p2a_no_channel_free_ack, QUIRK_P2A_NO_CHANNEL_FREE_ACK);
 
 	if (info->desc->ops->clear_channel)
 		info->desc->ops->clear_channel(cinfo);
-- 
